bug_report:
Post contracts are ignored on functions with no return statement.
This applies to void functions and coroutines (which usually have a return object but do not have a return statement).

e.g:
void foo (const int b) pre ( b == 9 )  // contract checked
{}
int main()
{
   foo(3);
}

void foo (const int b) post ( b == 9 )  // contract not checked
{}
int main()
{
   foo(3);
}

int foo (const int b) post ( b == 9 )  // contract checked
{
  return 1;
}
int main()
{
   foo(3);
}

======

I was expecting the original function body to be wrapped in a try/finally block with the post function as the cleanup.  Same back to 13.3 so it does not appear to be a regression.
